Wrapper code uniqueness: BlindCodeGenerator 12-char random; unique index backstop; on duplicate wrapper → conflict. Retry loop like blind code? Keep simple: try up to 5 times generating wrapper code on duplicate-wrapper duplicate key. But DuplicateKeyException from insertPickup could be uq_pickup_allocation (concurrent pickup same allocation) or uq_pickup_kit (shouldn't happen since experiment lock) or uq_pickup_wrapper. Since experiment row lock serializes pickups within the experiment, concurrency conflicts are minimal, but cross... all pickups are per-experiment locked. So duplicates only from wrapper collision (astronomically rare). I'll do a small retry loop for wrapper duplicates, mapping other duplicates to 409. Need to distinguish constraint names in H2 — the message contains constraint name like "uq_pickup_wrapper"? Existing code checks e.getMessage().contains("uq_allocation_participant") — H2 with DATABASE_TO_LOWER=TRUE lowercases constraint names, so contains works. I'll add helper methods in KitRepository: isDuplicateWrapper etc. Actually simpler: retry loop on any DuplicateKeyException from insertPickup that contains "uq_pickup_wrapper", else 409.

Note: markIssued happens before insertPickup; if insertPickup fails and we retry with new wrapper, markIssued already done — fine within same transaction; retry just re-inserts pickup with new wrapper code. But careful: if we retry the whole pickup insert, kit already issued — OK.

